{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nSplit from `floating-chromium-leafwing` (1f35-74fc-47a0-4d71), Decision 6 (operator-approved 2026-08-30). 1f35 was the stopgap: bound `anthropic` below the first httpx2-vendoring release (`<1`) so mirror-sweep legs stopped floating to SDKs whose `http_client` contract rejects a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`. The dependency boundary is `1.0.0`: `anthropic` 1.x (including the reproduced `1.2.0`) declares and validates `httpx2`, while `0.121.0` remains the pre-httpx2 line. This ticket is the approved long-term fix: adapt rebar's Anthropic provider seam for both contracts and widen the temporary cap.\n\n## Observed SDK contract evidence\n\n- `anthropic==1.2.0`: `inspect.signature(anthropic.AsyncAnthropic.__init__).parameters[\"http_client\"].annotation` prints `httpx2.AsyncClient | None`; constructing with stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient` raises `TypeError: Invalid http_client argument; Expected an instance of httpx2.AsyncClient but got <class 'httpx.AsyncClient'>`.\n- `anthropic==0.121.0`: the same annotation prints `httpx.AsyncClient | None`, so the pre-httpx2 path must stay stdlib-httpx compatible.\n- `anthropic==1.2.0` beta `messages.create` parameters include `extra_body` and `timeout`, but do **not** include `temperature`, `top_p`, or `top_k`; `anthropic==0.121.0` includes all three sampling kwargs and `extra_body`.\n- A local spike against `anthropic==1.2.0` showed `httpx2.AsyncClient(transport=httpx2.MockTransport(...))` is accepted and `extra_body={\"temperature\": 0.0}` is merged into the outbound JSON body as top-level `temperature`.\n- Inspection of the pinned pydantic-ai dispatch path shows `.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/pydantic_ai/models/anthropic.py:713` calls `self.client.beta.messages.create(...)` inside `_messages_create`; it is an instance-attribute lookup at request time, not a method captured at model construction.\n\n## Why this followed eb64 / 254e\n\nThe changed seam is `src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider`, inside epic `financial-stoneware-brant` (eb64-844b-ab7a-4915) and overlapping 254e. 254e's invariant is transport-owned retry: rebar supplies the HTTP client, sets `AsyncAnthropic(max_retries=0)`, retries transient 429/529/5xx plus timeout/network errors below the agent loop, honors positive `Retry-After`, and falls back to jitter. This fix preserves that invariant; it does not switch to SDK-managed retries.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Choose the type-detected custom-client branch because it is the branch compatible with 254e's `max_retries=0` transport-owned retry invariant.\n- Detect the SDK contract by reading `inspect.signature(AsyncAnthropic.__init__).parameters[\"http_client\"].annotation`; match annotation text containing `httpx2.AsyncClient`, which covers the observed 1.2.0 forward-ref/union string `httpx2.AsyncClient | None`. Default to stdlib `httpx` when the annotation is absent or ambiguous.\n- Build one shared `RetryConfig` and one shared `_validate_response` against the selected module. The retry predicate uses the selected module's `HTTPStatusError`, `TimeoutException`, and `NetworkError`; `_build_retry_wait` reads `exc.response.headers` generically, so the same Retry-After/jitter rules apply to both exception families.\n- For stdlib `httpx`, keep pydantic-ai's existing `AsyncTenacityTransport`. For `httpx2`, first check for a first-party `pydantic_ai.retries.HTTPX2TenacityTransport`; the current pinned pydantic-ai lacks it, so this patch uses a local `httpx2.AsyncBaseTransport` wrapper with the same retry/validate/close/context-manager behavior.\n- Handle Anthropic 1.x beta `messages.create` signature removal by wrapping the rebar-owned `anthropic_client.beta.messages.create` instance after provider construction. Pydantic-ai's `AnthropicModel._messages_create` dispatches every real request through `self.client.beta.messages.create(...)`, so late-binding that instance method is on the real request path. The wrapper moves unsupported real sampling kwargs (`temperature`, `top_p`, `top_k`) into `extra_body` and only drops `anthropic.Omit` placeholders. Upstream capability resolution still decides whether a model gets a real sampling value; the wrapper only changes the Python-call location required by the SDK signature. Provider-parity normalization reads the final wire JSON, where `extra_body` is merged into the top-level request body.\n- Widen `anthropic` to `>=0.121.0,<2`, keeping both pre-httpx2 and 1.x/httpx2 lines installable while excluding the next major line.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] `anthropic==1.2.0`: provider/model construction uses `httpx2.AsyncClient`, does not raise the old `TypeError`, and can issue a MockTransport request through `AnthropicProvider`/`AnthropicModel`.\n- [x] `anthropic==0.121.0`: provider/model construction remains compatible with stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`.\n- [x] 254e retry semantics are preserved for the selected HTTP module: retry predicate, Retry-After parsing, zero/expired-header fallback, jitter wait, and `max_retries=0` guard.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_transport_retry.py` covers httpx2 construction, retry, sampling-kwarg relocation through the real pydantic-ai `AnthropicModel` request path, and a spy guard that fails if pydantic-ai stops dispatching through the late-bound `client.beta.messages.create` instance method.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_transport_retry_jitter.py` remains green for `_build_retry_wait`'s shared Retry-After/jitter contract.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_provider_parity.py` captures direct-Anthropic requests through the SDK-selected transport module and confirms sampling values remain visible in the normalized wire payload.\n- [x] Existing direct-Anthropic MockTransport harnesses are updated to patch the SDK-selected transport module in `tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py`, `tests/unit/test_agentic_message_cache.py`, `tests/unit/test_llm_provider_factory.py`, `tests/unit/test_llm_timeouts.py`, `tests/unit/test_cache_prefix_breakpoint.py`, `tests/unit/test_candidate_tracing.py`, `tests/unit/test_candidate_tracing_oracle.py`, and `tests/unit/test_llm_config_gate_root.py`.\n- [x] `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` proves `0.121.0` and `1.2.0` are allowed while `2.0.0` is rejected.\n- [x] Portable across CI providers / no CI: the adaptation is local Python plus dependency bounds; no provider-specific CI trigger is required."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788241405189973001,"uuid":"dc3bfd0c-d4ec-47aa-8bc8-687e4100f266"}